Parked 2026-08-10: instance destroyed 2026-08-08. Rebuild blocked on Aheeva license hostid + missing VPC BPA exclusion + unresolved public_subnet_id sharing question.

WHY THIS LEAF IS PARKED
=======================
On 2026-08-08 the CI fan-out apply for WAF PR #59 destroyed this leaf's EC2
instance (i-04dc1a79b8277f654). Since then the leaf fails on every module-level
PR with:

  Error: creating EC2 Instance: ... InvalidSubnetID.NotFound:
  The subnet ID 'subnet-0919739a39165a934' does not exist

That is harmless in itself (there is nothing left to destroy, it only fails to
create) but it turns every subsequent module PR red. A permanently-red pipeline
trains people to ignore failures, which is how the original destruction went
unnoticed. So the leaf is parked rather than left failing.

Parking is CI-only. It does not touch state or any AWS resource. `detect` skips
any leaf containing this file; delete the file and the leaf is live again.

ROOT CAUSE — CORRECTED 2026-09-08
=================================
Earlier revisions of this file blamed "an ami_id updated in tfvars but never
applied". That was wrong: the module carries `ignore_changes = [ami]`, so an
AMI diff cannot force replacement. The stale subnet was also not the cause.

The retained plan log (run 31279439349, job 93158288989) has exactly ONE line
marked `# forces replacement`:

  ~ associate_public_ip_address = true -> false # forces replacement

The ec2-migrated module set `associate_public_ip_address = false` as a
launch-time instruction, but the provider reads it back as a steady-state fact.
Once EIP 3.16.53.180 was attached on 2026-07-07, the instance refreshed as
`true`, and the attribute forces replacement — so this leaf silently carried a
queued destroy+create for a month. PR #59 touched terraform/modules/**, the
fan-out applied every leaf, and the queued replacement executed.

There were therefore TWO independent faults:
  1. associate_public_ip_address  -> why the instance was DESTROYED.
  2. InvalidSubnetID.NotFound     -> why the recreate FAILED.

Fault 1 is fixed: `associate_public_ip_address` is now in the module's
`ignore_changes` list. Do not remove it. Fault 2 is still open (below).

Full postmortem: .kiro/journal/2026-08-08-cti-v7-destroyed-by-module-fanout.md

WHAT IS BLOCKING THE REBUILD
============================
1. Aheeva license hostid. The in-flight license reissue was keyed to hostid
   02417393bdd5, which died with the instance. A rebuilt instance gets a new
   hostid. Aheeva has to confirm they can rebind before we burn another one.
   This is the long-lead item — it gates everything else.

2. VPC Block Public Access exclusion. Option B needs one for the public subnet,
   and `describe-vpc-block-public-access-exclusions` in Production returns
   empty. See docs/07-Operations/cti-v7-lza-exception.md. LZA change, delivered
   as a config zip upload (see .kiro/steering/lza-config-zip-delivery.md).

3. RESOLVED 2026-09-10 — the subnet question is settled and tfvars is corrected
   (PR #97). public_subnet_id is now subnet-08ce7fb6c30eed107 (10.12.0.192/27),
   recreated by the LZA pipeline on 2026-09-10 and verified visible from the
   Production account via TerraformExecution — i.e. the RAM share is live.

   For the record, the 2026-08-14 duplicate-Name mystery is explained. The
   original subnet-0919739a39165a934 (10.12.0.32/27) held cti-v7 until
   2026-08-08. LZA had recreated public-a as subnet-0dc7b70d38275e775, which
   orphaned ...9165a934 — it survived only because cti-v7's ENI was still
   attached — and dropped its RAM share to Production. That is why RunInstances
   failed with InvalidSubnetID.NotFound: the ID was never stale, the SHARE was
   gone.

   DO NOT USE EITHER OLD ID:
     subnet-0919739a39165a934  empty orphan, retagged ORPHANED-do-not-use-*,
                               not shared to Production. Cannot be deleted -
                               ec2:DeleteSubnet is SCP-denied.
     subnet-0dc7b70d38275e775  DELETED 2026-09-04 by the config-zip incident.

WHAT IS ALREADY KNOWN GOOD
==========================
- EIP 3.16.53.180 (eipalloc-02826934c621235e9) SURVIVED, unassociated. The
  Aheeva vendor allowlist for that IP is still valid, and no re-allocation is
  needed (ec2:AllocateAddress is SCP-denied without the exception).
- subnet-08ce7fb6c30eed107 (the CURRENT public-a) is Option-B-capable, verified
  2026-09-10: route table rtb-084d7813ef4ae10d8 carries 0.0.0.0/0 ->
  igw-0e732e2a82da6dc5a and 10.0.0.0/8 -> tgw-0360ed77a03707835, 27 free IPs,
  us-east-2a, MapPublicIpOnLaunch = False (correct - the EIP supplies the public
  IP, not subnet auto-assign). Note the IGW id changed too; the old
  igw-010871f4083a631af reference is stale.
- AMI ami-0289fff8a491f450a (cti-v7-clean) is intact. The rebuild starts there.
- The destroyed root volume is NOT recoverable: delete_on_termination was true
  and the leaf has no BackupPlan tag, so nothing is in the LZA backup vault.
  The sip.conf externip work has to be redone.

TO UNPARK
=========
1. Get the Aheeva answer on hostid rebinding. Do not rebuild before this.
   THIS IS NOW THE ONLY LONG-LEAD BLOCKER.
2. Land the VPC BPA exclusion for subnet-08ce7fb6c30eed107 specifically.
3. DONE 2026-09-10 (PR #97) — tfvars points at subnet-08ce7fb6c30eed107 and the
   RAM share to Production is verified live. Nothing further needed.
4. Add a `BackupPlan = Continuous` tag to the leaf's tags block BEFORE the
   rebuild, so the hand-configuration lands in the LZA backup vault this time.
   Root volume is delete_on_termination = true and that is not changing.
5. Confirm the module still has `associate_public_ip_address` in its
   `ignore_changes` list. If it does not, STOP — re-adding it is a
   prerequisite, or the rebuilt instance will be destroyed on the next apply
   exactly as it was on 2026-08-08.
6. Delete this file.
7. Open a PR for the leaf. Expect a CREATE, not a replacement — there is no
   instance in state. If the plan shows any destroy or replace, stop and work
   out why; do not add ALLOW-DESTROY to get past it.
8. Re-associate the surviving EIP, then redo the sip.conf externip work and the
   RLM license bring-up per docs/07-Operations/cti-v7-wave2-runbook.md Part 7.
